{
  "dom_id": "step-146053",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Finding the Roots of a Function Given a Mapping Diagram",
  "problem": "What are the roots of the function $g(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190079/assets/951e37aa910fa9cf3588ee047dd6258f8e628198ce3ce4620119d4b30bee8c8d.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $g(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that $g(9) = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the only root of the function is $x=9.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
